Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:39:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Shim: the pluggable_backend branch's current plugin names

keras@pluggable_backend (head 60be5d35, 2026-09-17) resolves a plugin's
layer / export modules with `find_spec` and reads fixed attribute names:
`getattr(keras_<name>.src.layer, "BackendLayer")` and
`getattr(keras_<name>.src.export, "SavedModelExportArchive")`; a missing
module falls back to an empty BackendLayer / the
BaseSavedModelExportArchive. The shim exported `Layer` / `TinygradLayer`
and `ExportArchive` / `TinygradExportArchive`, so both getattrs failed
at `import keras` on the branch.

`BackendLayer` is added next to the older names. `src/export.py` is
removed instead of renamed: keras-openvino and keras-mlx (the split-out
reference packages) ship no export module either, and the base fallback
raises the same loud NotImplementedError for both backend hooks that the
tinygrad archive did. The stock (hook) path is untouched: it serves
`_backend/export.py`, not the shim.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C81VdRop6BGDx986cZKWmo
